      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DOLLY (8) is the one to beat after an understandable 11th in a BM64 at Kembla Grange, where she faced interference in the straight and was beaten just over five lengths. Her previous win in a CL3 at this track is key, as she came from well back to beat Steve's Way. Can sit closer this time and return to winning ways. KEIKOKU (1) has consistent form, running second at Moruya and fifth at Canberra, where he was tightened near the 450m. Out in trip now looks a very good move and Loy reuniting is a positive sign. Can bounce back to his best form. CANNY HELL (4) was solid late in a BM74 at Wagga, better suited back to a track-and-distance where he has a win and a placing from three attempts. COCO DE LUXE (10) finished third to DOLLY here when the race favourite before having issues at Wangaratta. Back to this scenario looks suitable. GREATHAM BOY (2) can improve on the fresh performance.",
